    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1f0a227_b3181ff9",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bd9995x.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 810,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-20T20:33:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What determines what vsysreg should be set to? I see we\u0027re just writing values above, but why would we do that w/o understanding the state of the battery?\n\nThere\u0027s concern that this patch will just push over current conditions off to the adapter itself. Why disable input current entirely? Shouldn\u0027t we be able to boot far enough to negotiate what the real current limit should be?",
      "revId": "867f8ad26931647a8e19edd5e583b3789f203a5b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b68ec163_ab84fd8d",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bd9995x.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 810,
      "author": {
        "id": 1128369
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-20T22:00:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Battery voltage determines the value what VSYS register can be set to. At init, we want the charge state machine to be at pre-charge state. We take the battery voltage max (which is const) hence we can ignore battery state.\n\nDefault input current limit is 1.472A. We are setting correct VSYS at init hence charger can cut the power if it detects VSYS over voltage (VSYS_OVP \u003d VSYS * 1.15).\nFrom the datasheet we are disabling the input current limiting only when VBAT is dead battery.\nYes, but if we dont have enough power in the battery charger will cut the input current hence system won\u0027t boot.",
      "parentUuid": "c1f0a227_b3181ff9",
      "revId": "867f8ad26931647a8e19edd5e583b3789f203a5b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9be2b1e_1b13be1f",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bd9995x.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 810,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-21T01:07:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sounds like this is a fix for 35647661 not for 35648317. You seem to be suggesting we revert the fix for 35647661 (so we unbreak 35648317 by disabling IADP). Is it right?\n\nI think we also should clear BD9995X_CMD_VIN_CTRL_SET_VSYS_PRIORITY once we know battery voltage is high enough for vsys to drive the system. Where do we clear it?",
      "parentUuid": "b68ec163_ab84fd8d",
      "revId": "867f8ad26931647a8e19edd5e583b3789f203a5b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8e03588_3bd35f87",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bd9995x.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 810,
      "author": {
        "id": 1128369
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-03-21T01:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fix for both 35648317 \u0026 35647661. Yes, we dont have to revert IADP enable fix.\nWe can keep VSYS_PRIORITY\u003d1 always, as input current limiting is disabled only when VBAT is \u003c VSYSREG_SET.",
      "parentUuid": "d9be2b1e_1b13be1f",
      "revId": "867f8ad26931647a8e19edd5e583b3789f203a5b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
